{
  "$description": "Semantic tier, dark theme.\n\nStatus colours are re-tuned rather than reused. The light-mode values do not hold contrast on a dark surface, and critical must stay unmistakable \u2014 so each hue moves to a lighter step and each surface tint moves to the ink-composited version. Same key space as light; the build fails if a key is missing.",
  "bg": {
    "$type": "color",
    "$value": "{ref.ink.950}"
  },
  "bg-subtle": {
    "$type": "color",
    "$value": "{ref.ink.900}"
  },
  "bg-muted": {
    "$type": "color",
    "$value": "{ref.ink.820}"
  },
  "surface": {
    "$type": "color",
    "$value": "{ref.ink.860}"
  },
  "surface-raised": {
    "$type": "color",
    "$value": "{ref.ink.780}"
  },
  "surface-overlay": {
    "$type": "color",
    "$value": "{ref.ink.740}",
    "$description": "Was #1d263000 in the hand-written file \u2014 an eight-digit hex with a zero alpha, which made every overlay surface fully transparent. Popovers and dialogs rendered with the page showing through. Fixed here at the source."
  },
  "border": {
    "$type": "color",
    "$value": "{ref.ink.700}"
  },
  "$comment-border-strong": "ink.600 measured 2.02:1 on the dark ground, below the 3:1 floor for a field border. ink.500 is 3.21:1.",
  "border-strong": {
    "$type": "color",
    "$value": "{ref.ink.500}"
  },
  "text": {
    "$type": "color",
    "$value": "{ref.ink.100}"
  },
  "text-muted": {
    "$type": "color",
    "$value": "{ref.ink.200}"
  },
  "text-subtle": {
    "$type": "color",
    "$value": "{ref.ink.300}"
  },
  "text-on-accent": {
    "$type": "color",
    "$value": "{ref.ink.on-accent}"
  },
  "text-on-fill": {
    "$type": "color",
    "$value": "{ref.white}",
    "$description": "A label on a filled neutral \u2014 the Switch's off track, which is {border-strong} in every theme and therefore a mid-grey in every theme. Separate from text-on-accent because that one follows the accent, and the dark accent is light: pointing the off label at it put #071014 on #5d6c7e at 3.57:1. White clears AA on border-strong in all three themes, and the pair is in the contrast gate so it stays that way."
  },
  "$comment-accent": "brand.300, not cyan.300. The dark tier used to reach for a hue the brand does not contain, so the same product was teal-green in light and cyan in dark \u2014 a difference nobody chose and everybody saw. brand.300 measures 12.74:1 for text-on-accent and 12.91:1 on bg, against cyan.300's 13.25 and 13.42: the same step of a different ramp, and the floors are untouched.",
  "accent": {
    "$type": "color",
    "$value": "{ref.brand.300}"
  },
